# tally 2.1.8 R16 (pick P29 on #175's p6win), L §4.6 and §4.4: a reading after save, whose day is window(03-16, 03-25),
# isn't applied before the window (03-10: 1 050.00 PLN); inside it the balance is the window's hole (03-20); from
# its last day on it is the reading plus what is booked since, the same for every day of the window, since nothing
# else touches konto inside it (04-20, 05-31: 90.00 PLN). 2.1.8's first refcore left every later day the hole.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place sav: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input keep: money PLN
input d_save: date
input go: bool

move save: transfers
  on d_save
  reads konto
  when go
  leg cash from konto to sav amount max(0 PLN, bal(konto) - keep)

move mm[m in months]: transfers
  on end_of(m) - 1 day
  reads konto
  leg cash from konto to sav amount max(0 PLN, bal(konto) - keep)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  keep = 100.00 PLN "s"
  d_save = window(2026-03-16, 2026-03-25) "s"
  go = true "s"
  opening[konto] = 1050.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
  opening[sav] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"

version st
  cite s
  governs 2026-03..2026-05
  known 2026-01-02
  anchor konto
  stated[konto] = 90.00 PLN after save "saldo"

ask b: bal(konto, 2026-03-10), bal(konto, 2026-03-20), bal(konto, 2026-04-20), bal(konto, 2026-05-31)
ask g: last(stated[konto], 2026-05-31)
=== expect
b: (1 050.00 PLN, ?"date within window(2026-03-16, 2026-03-25) not precise enough for the day of save" (save), 90.00 PLN, 90.00 PLN)
  anchor: konto after save, stated 90.00 PLN, difference ?"date within window(2026-03-16, 2026-03-25) not precise enough for the day of save" (save)
  cut 2026-06-10
g: 90.00 PLN
  held: stated[konto] = 90.00 PLN (st), read for 2026-05-31
  cut 2026-06-10
warning: WARN-UNREAD place world is read by nothing
